module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.AtlasCovering
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Chow.FlatPullbackOrderOfVanishing
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Chow.KeyFormulaChart.EtaleStalkOrder
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Decent.HenselianLocalRingMap
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Decent.HenselianLocalRingMapAffine

/-!
# The map of henselian local rings induced by an étale morphism is unramified

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be an **étale** morphism of decent algebraic spaces over `S` and let `x` be a
point of `X`. `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_henselianLocalRingHom_chartSquare` produces a
local homomorphism `φ : 𝒪^h_{Y, f(x)} ⟶ 𝒪^h_{X, x}` together with the commuting square of
pointed étale charts that exhibits it as the one `f` induces. This file adds one conclusion to
that statement: `φ` is **unramified**, i.e.

  `𝔪_{𝒪^h_{Y, f(x)}} · 𝒪^h_{X, x} = 𝔪_{𝒪^h_{X, x}}`.

That identity is what makes the multiplicity
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.primeDivisorFlatMultiplicity` of a prime divisor over its image equal
to one, and so what turns `ord_Z(g ∘ f) = m · ord_{Z'}(g)` of Stacks 0EQA into an equality of
orders of vanishing. A comment of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/Chow/EtalePullbackPrincipalDivisor.lean` records the
identity as "not in this repository"; for an étale `f` — in particular for an isomorphism — it
is proved here.

## The proof

The chart square gives an elementary étale neighbourhood `V` of `f(x)` in `Y`, an elementary
étale neighbourhood `U` of `x` in `X`, a morphism of schemes `j : U ⟶ V` over `f` carrying the
distinguished point to the distinguished point, and the compatibility of `φ` with the stalk map
`α : 𝒪_{V, v} ⟶ 𝒪_{U, u}` of that square along the canonical maps of Stacks 0EMY. Three
ingredients then close the argument.

* `j` is étale. The chart `U ⟶ X` of the neighbourhood is étale and so is `f`, so `U ⟶ Y` is
  étale; `V ⟶ Y` is étale; and the square identifies `j ≫ (V ⟶ Y)` with `U ⟶ Y`. This is the
  *cancellation* of étaleness, Stacks 03FV, in the form
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etale_of_etaleChart_square`. Note that no surjectivity of `j` is
  needed: the cancellation used is the one valid for an arbitrary morphism of étale charts.
* Hence `α` is unramified: that is Stacks 00UW for the stalk map of an étale morphism of
  schemes, `AlgebraicGeometry.map_maximalIdeal_stalkMap_of_etale`, transported across the
  comparison of the stalks of `V` at `v` and at `j(u)`, which is an isomorphism.
* And each of `𝒪^h_{Y, f(x)}`, `𝒪^h_{X, x}` has its maximal ideal generated by the image of the
  maximal ideal of the corresponding chart stalk, because it is a henselization of it:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_maximalIdeal_stalkToHenselianLocalRing`.

Pushing `𝔪_{𝒪_{V, v}}` forward along the two equal composites
`φ ∘ (𝒪_{V, v} → 𝒪^h_{Y, f(x)})` and `(𝒪_{U, u} → 𝒪^h_{X, x}) ∘ α` gives the identity.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_maximalIdeal_chartStalkMap_of_etale`: the stalk map of a pointed
  morphism of schemes which is étale extends the maximal ideal to the maximal ideal, in the
  spelling `exists_henselianLocalRingHom_chartSquare` uses (through the comparison of stalks).
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.etale_chartSquare_of_isEtale`: the morphism of charts over an étale
  morphism of algebraic spaces is étale.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.map_maximalIdeal_of_chartSquare`: unramifiedness of `φ` from the
  chart square, with étaleness of `j` as the hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_henselianLocalRingHom_chartSquare_map_maximalIdeal_of_isEtale`:
  `exists_henselianLocalRingHom_affineChartSquare` for an étale morphism, with unramifiedness
  of `φ` added to its conclusions.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_henselianLocalRingHom_map_maximalIdeal_of_isEtale`: the same
  with the chart square forgotten.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 00UW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00UW)
